WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.239
- Every morning I wake
up and I make pretend

00:00:02.239 --> 00:00:05.016
that my mother, or children, or wife die.

00:00:05.016 --> 00:00:07.599
(gentle music)

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.920
The only consistent in my life

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.270
has been perspective and gratitude,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.760
it's the only consistent in my life.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.180
Every morning I wake up and make pretend

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.680
that my mother, or children, or wife die.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.750
I promise you, if you're
in touch with your feelings

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.390
and you can trick yourself to feel it,

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.223
even right now I felt it a little bit

00:00:33.223 --> 00:00:35.230
and it really fuckin' hurts,

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.350
like, nothing else matters.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.800
I'm completely driven by gratitude.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.370
I keep things in very simple perspective.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.700
I'm thrilled and very in tune with my ego.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.530
I'm also very thrilled and
in tune with my humility.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.470
I think I'm the best

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.220
and I think that if I disappear tomorrow

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.490
nobody really gives a shit.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.770
And so, that yin and yang
is very important to me,

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.270
and so what I do consistently,

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:03.270
and have for 30 years now, is
I keep things in perspective.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.263
I want legacy.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.330
I think the reason I'm liked is 'cause

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.670
I'll reply to somebody, who says

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.880
they're on their way here to see me talk,

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.883
on twitter and reply to her.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.490
I'm playing a different game, I ...

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.010
Tyler is filming today's Daily Vee,

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.590
I met with a former employee

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.470
and he flat out broke the wall

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.947
and he was like, "Dude,
I just have to ask you,

00:01:25.947 --> 00:01:27.687
"why did you take that meeting?

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.807
"It's a former employee,
one that you fired,

00:01:30.807 --> 00:01:32.427
"one that came to tell
you that they were sorry

00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:35.497
"for not getting it,
she pitched you stuff.

00:01:35.497 --> 00:01:37.297
"You didn't get anything out of it."

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.100
He said, "Why'd you do that?"

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.637
And I said, "Because making money

00:01:41.637 --> 00:01:43.280
"isn't the only thing that interests me."

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.140
I love the process more than
the riches and the fames.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.950
When people ask me, "When
are you gonna buy the Jets?"

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.650
and I always say 25 years from now,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.586
they're disappointed, I'm pumped.

00:01:51.586 --> 00:01:53.540
(laughing)

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.503
It's amazing to me.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:56.930
They're literally disappointed.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.462
I'm like, "It's $3 billon,
I have work to do."

00:01:59.462 --> 00:02:00.400
(laughing)

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.020
I'm not crippled by the current

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.793
political correctness of parenting.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.250
You're looking at a kid
who didn't see his dad

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.450
until he was 14 years old and we have

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.410
the greatest relationship
of all-time and I love him.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.800
And he slept home every single night

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.330
but I never saw him once.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.660
That doesn't mean my workaholic nature

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.930
will work for me and my kids,
I don't take that for granted.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.850
I think that you need
to know how to breathe.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.380
I know what makes me breathe.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.100
My family makes me breathe,

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.833
but I've gotta do what I wanna do.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.700
Like, I have to.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:28.720
I'll just break.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.260
Everybody in here has
different work/life balance.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.650
You also have different work/life balance

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.700
at different times in your life.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.400
I don't think you find balance

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.960
in any other way than your own balance,

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.960
and I think that over-communication
with your partner

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.430
and the variables in that
relationship are the key.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.290
I'm working harder, right this second,

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.520
than I ever have in my entire life.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.740
That's why I started Daily Vee,

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.270
just wanted to put all of you on notice

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.510
like, you're not working as hard as I am.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.560
And, I wanted to do that

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.740
because people think they're
putting in enough work,

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.573
they're just not.

00:03:00.573 --> 00:03:03.050
Everybody's talking shit,
everybody loves to hit me up,

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:03.960
Gary Vee hustling.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:04.800
I look at their account

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.736
and they're playing ping pong at 4:30.

00:03:06.736 --> 00:03:08.726
(laughing)

00:03:08.726 --> 00:03:10.380
I mean, people don't
understand what hustle is.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.920
I took one vacation in my 20s,
but I have crazy aspiration.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.270
You should take 11, but
don't come telling me

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.280
you're gonna by the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.940
So, people get my message confused.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:21.980
They're like, "You're
always talking about hustle,

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:22.813
where's life?"

00:03:22.813 --> 00:03:24.530
I'm like, "No, no, no, no, no, no, no!"

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.070
If you're a hundred
percent happy, like I am,

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.810
then I got no advice for
you, you figured it out.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.900
So, when my rich friends complain to me

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.670
about not spending enough
time with their family,

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.820
they're real easy to give advice to, too,

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.470
spend more time with your family.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.140
This shit is binary,
this stuff is so basic,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.450
we complicate it.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.010
And, I'm happy when people have ambitions

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.840
that allow them to work 40 hours a week

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.860
and they're thrilled, I have to move fast.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.320
Like everybody tells me Vander

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.590
was not gonna be successful
if I move too fast.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.980
They were wrong, 'cause I'm fast.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.310
Let's play out the scenario.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.490
I grew too fast, I
couldn't afford my staff,

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:03.340
I had to cut people

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.300
then people got scared we weren't stable,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.650
they quit and my shit got fucked up.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.370
That's scary of going too fast.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.440
Let me tell you what
happens way more often.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.660
90% of this room is going too slow

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.350
and has left tons of money on the table

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.240
but they don't know it 'cause it's hidden.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.810
It's not obvious to anybody
if you're doing a million

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.070
but you should be doing three million

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.380
but you're going too slow.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.627
I mean, I love when everybody's like,

00:04:25.627 --> 00:04:26.950
"Well, it's easy for you."

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.340
It wasn't always.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.380
Like, you weren't with
me when I was in my house

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.430
printing on that slow-ass computer.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.300
Ya know, 20% off a case of wine

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.530
and then I grab the whole thing

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.530
and then I, fuckin', woke up at 6 a.m.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.710
And went to the Short Hills Mall

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.120
and just went and put that on the flyer.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.130
You weren't with me.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.820
People think things are below them.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.040
I still don't think things are below me.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.410
Like, nothing is below
me, I'll do anything.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:49.640
And so, the first thing

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.110
is figure out who you
are and what you want,

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.380
and then deploy real self-awareness.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.977
But, I'm telling you, the
thing that I'm fearful of

00:04:55.977 --> 00:04:58.830
and the reason I didn't
step off stage yet is,

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:02.710
it's been so good for almost
a decade, this has been easy.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.000
There's so much money out there,

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.450
everybody's getting money
for their dumb ideas

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:08.650
that make no money.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:09.890
People are getting funded for everything,

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.030
so if you haven't been able
to figure out how to get money

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.343
you're a triple loser.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.350
So the way to answer that,
and punch me in the face

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.660
and tell me that you're
not, is go make money

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.990
instead of dwelling why
you haven't raised it.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.680
I promise you something about money,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.853
money's real funny, real funny,

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.310
money doesn't care what you look like.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.843
Here's most people's strategies in life.

00:05:34.568 --> 00:05:35.470
(laughing)

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.780
if you are not capable,
in 2017, to Google shit

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.630
and figure out what's going
on in the world, fuck you.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:43.963
We have to start getting into meritocracy.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.750
Somebody should lose if they're not seeing

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.400
where the puck is going.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.210
If you drivin' a truck,
today, you know it's coming.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.960
You've heard it, somebody told you.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.700
So, either, you take it seriously

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:59.143
and you start educating
yourself or you don't.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.690
That's the game.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.950
That's life and that's the historic nature

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.250
of human beings forever.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.020
So, just 'cause we're, now, living

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.310
and it's our turn to go through something,

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.820
this has always happened.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.350
I don't see truck driver Johnny

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.630
feeling bad for Rick the bookstore owner

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:17.920
'cause Amazon came along.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:21.200
This is the first time that
innovation fucked shit up.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.060
Nobody's cryin' for the
farmers in middle America.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:25.980
Nobody's cryin' for the
people, in Cleveland,

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.350
who own the docks.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.570
And so, what 55 year
old Charles has to do,

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.660
when he is out of a
job, is get another job

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.440
whatever that job is.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.700
So if Charles is smart and has skills

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.880
he's teaching himself something now

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.360
to be ready for three years from now.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.240
But, Charles wants to watch football.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:49.660
Here's the punchline,
the market is the market.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.400
What is the 54 year old gonna do, adjust

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.917
or lose?

00:06:55.917 --> 00:06:58.584
(gentle music)

